"It looks rather muddy down here."

I noticed that bug myself when I tried to change blue to lt. blue.
(I nethack from an easy chair, with the monitor about 2 feet away,
so the dark blue was hard to pick out at that distance.)

I finally determined that the docs on this in the version of msdos.hlp
included with the official linc PC binaries were incorrect.  They
included white as one of the colors in the middle of the list, while
the code didn't expect it.  Deleting the entry for white (15, II belive)
in the videocolors option line solved the problem for me.

I reported it to nethack-bugs, so the Dev. Team should be aware of it,
assuming my mail reached them.  Interestingly enough, the version of
msdos.hlp on my unix machine is correct, I believe, and is the same as
the line given above, and has an earlier timestamp than the same file in
the linc distrbution.  Go figure.

